{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]As [D]with [Am]glad[G]ness [C]men [Cm]of [Gsus]old[G]
[Am]Did [D7]the [G]guid[Em]ing [Dsus7]star be[G]hold,
[Em]As with [Am]joy [Em]they [Cm]hailed its [Bm7]ligh[Bdim]t,
[C]Lead[Cdim]ing[G]on[C]ward, [D2]beam[D]ing [G]bright,
[B]So, [B7]most [Em7]gracious [C7]Lor[Dm7]d, may [G]we[G7]
[C]Ev[Cdim]er [G]more [Am7]be[Bm]led [D7]to [G]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G][D]As [Am]with [G]joyful [C][Cm]steps [Gsus]they [G]sped
[Am][D7]To [G]that [Em]lowly [Dsus7]manger [G]bed,
[Em]There [Am]to [Em]bend [Cm]the [Bm7]knee [Bdim]before
[C][Cdim]Him [G]whom [C]heav'n [D2]and [D]earth [G]adore,
[B][B7]So [Em7]may [C7]we [Dm7]with [G]willing [G7]feet
[C][Cdim]Ever [G]seek [Am7][Bm]Thy [D7]mercy [G]seat.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G][D]As [Am]they [G]offered [C][Cm]gifts [Gsus]most [G]rare
[Am]At [D7]that [G]manger [Em]rude [Dsus7]and [G]bare,
[Em]So [Am]may [Em]we [Cm]with [Bm7]holy [Bdim]joy,
[C][Cdim]Pure, [G]and [C]free [D2]from [D]sin's [G]alloy,
[B][B7]All [Em7]our [C7][Dm7]costliest [G]treasures [G7]bring,
[C][Cdim]Christ, [G]to [Am7]Thee [Bm]our [D7]heav'nly [G]King.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G][D]Holy [Am][G]Jesus, [C][Cm]every [Gsus][G]day
[Am]Keep [D7]us [G]in [Em]the [Dsus7]narrow [G]way;
[Em]And, [Am]when [Em]earthly [Cm]things [Bm7]are [Bdim]past,
[C][Cdim]Bring [G]our [C]ransomed [D2]souls [D]at [G]last
[B]Where [B7]they [Em7]need [C7]no [Dm7]star [G]to [G7]guide,
[C][Cdim]Where [G]no [Am7]clouds [Bm]Thy [D7]glory [G]hide.
{end_of_verse}
